-- title:
--   Non-Eisenstein corners of H¹(Γ₀(N),𝒪) are parabolic
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$, let $S$ be a set of natural numbers, let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring and let $k$ be a field that is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra. Write $H^1 = \mathrm{Hom}(\mathrm{Additive}\,\Gamma_H(N,\top),\mathcal{O})$, the additive homomorphisms from $\Gamma_H(N,\top)=\Gamma_0(N)$ (the subgroup $H=\top$ of $(\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$ being everything) to $\mathcal{O}$; it carries the family of endomorphisms [`CohCarrier.opFamily`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) indexed by the generators $T_\ell$ (for primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$), $U_q$ (for primes $q\mid N$) and $\langle d\rangle$ (for $d\in(\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$), the first two acting by `heckeTL` and the last by `diamondL`. Assume these endomorphisms commute pairwise, and fix an arbitrary function $\bar\theta$ from the generators to $k$; let $B\subseteq \mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}}(H^1)$ be the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra generated by the image of the family. Let $Sp$ be an idempotent splitting of $B$: a number $n$, elements $e_0,\dots,e_{n-1}$ forming a complete orthogonal set of idempotents, and ideals $\mathfrak{m}_0,\dots,\mathfrak{m}_{n-1}$, each maximal, exhausting the maximal ideals of $B$, with $e_i\in\mathfrak{m}_j$ exactly when $i\ne j$. Fix an index $i_0$ and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid N$ and $\ell\equiv 1 \pmod t$ for every $t$ with $t^2\mid N$, and assume $T_\ell-(\ell+1)\notin\mathfrak{m}_{i_0}$ in $B$. Then every $\varphi$ in the corner submodule $e_{i_0}H^1$ (the range of multiplication by $e_{i_0}$ on $H^1$) lies in [`ModularCurve.Period.parabolicHoms`](def/ModularCurve_PeriodMap.html#L62), i.e. $\varphi(\gamma)=0$ for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(N)$ whose matrix has $\mathrm{tr}(\gamma)^2=4$.
--
--   This is the cohomological form of the statement that at a non-Eisenstein maximal ideal of the Hecke algebra the boundary part of the cohomology of the open modular curve dies, so that the full group cohomology of $\Gamma_0(N)$ may be used in place of parabolic cohomology (Darmon–Diamond–Taylor, Lemma 4.13(c)). It is used by the constructions of corner realisations and of the rungs relating levels in the Hecke-local part of the modularity-lifting argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CohCarrier_mem_parabolicHoms_of_mem_cornerSubmodule_H1_of_notMem.lean

